- [P2] Scope final witnesses to the mapped network — /Users/cunxiy/Documents/research/autoresearch-eda/abc-harness/src/map/scl/sclSize.c:693-693
  When `stmap64` records at least one witness, the records live in mapper-wide globals until the next `stime`, and this unconditional hook does not check that the timed network is the stmap64 result or derived from it. If the user loads a different mapped design before timing, or the final remap fails after seeds were recorded, the next `stime` matches stale AIG ids against that unrelated network and emits bogus `stmap64 final-witness` rows. The witness state should be cleared on those paths or associated with the network lineage being timed.
