  When a cut-only seed is for an AIG whose opposite phase is also mapped, this records only `Stmap56NodeAigId` even though `fPhase` distinguishes the actual literal, and the final witness scan compares only the AIG id. In that scenario `stime` can attach the seed to the opposite-polarity gate and report the wrong load/criticality; carry the literal or phase through the witness record and match on it.
